      "pingZeNote": "North of Solitary Hill Temple and west of Jia Pavilion, the water lies level beneath low-hanging clouds. Early orioles vie for sunlit boughs; new swallows peck spring mud. Riotous blossoms begin to dazzle the eyes; tender grass barely covers horse hooves. Most beloved is the eastern shore where walks never suffice, along White Sand Causeway shaded by green willows.",
